sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront somite segmentation faithfully reproduces Xenopus laevis & Gallus gallus vertebrate paraxial mesoderm somites morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Xenopus laevis & Gallus gallus vertebrate paraxial mesoderm somites specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-clock-and-wavefront-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py; output: docs/media/clock_and_wavefront_comparison.png; organism: Xenopus laevis & Gallus gallus vertebrate paraxial mesoderm somites; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: c943fd8ec360d2fc8a2730571fb91c8337ae0de4cb262a0f6d695d053bbbcf13; artifact_sha256: 0a6c41da9df6f972bcba0ce2571dcdaa3d70ec1a69a8067f3c712f3fcb054a1c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/clock_and_wavefront/clock_and_wavefront_reference.json=4851550f4179ae63..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/fgf_ra_vertex_reference.json=1dedf71c930b5ed0..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=0beabd3277c705e6..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/somite_embryo_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-clock-and-wavefront-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cooke & Zeeman (1976) J. Theor. Biol. 58:455-476 kinematic somite wavelength law S = v * T_c and Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe wavefront manifold | Cooke (1975) Nature 254:196-199 Xenopus laevis blastula size-reduction invariance (N ~ 40 somites across normal and miniature embryos) | Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508: mutual FGF/RA inhibition is bistable and its switching threshold defines a sharp determination front that moves with axis elongation; Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422: the fgf8 gradient is set by mRNA decay in cells leaving the tailbud | Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232: an ectopic FGF8 bead produces smaller somites at its level (no numerical ratio reported) | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Curr. Biol. 17:2095-2104 vertex-model energy and case-I parameters; Bi et al. (2015) Nat. Phys. 11:1074-1079 shape-index rigidity transition p0* = 3.81; reconstructed_in_script: 1D anteroposterior Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe ODE tau_chi*dchi/dt = -(chi^3 - a(x,t)*chi - b_osc(x,t)) with either the prescribed kinematic front a = tanh((v t - x)/sigma_w) or the Goldbeter FGF/RA toggle front a = tanh((R - F)/kappa_a), m = F^4/(F^4 + K_mob^4), driven by tailbud elongation through M_F = exp(-(x_tb - x)/lambda_F), lambda_F = v_tb/k_dM (reduced two-variable toggle; Cyp26/Raldh2 lumped) | Endogenous front velocity fit (v_front = 2.22222 um/min vs v_tb = 2.2222, R^2 = 1.000), 4-point v_tb sweep (S RMSE 0.09 um), decaying-Gaussian FGF8 bead perturbation (min adjacent somite ratio 0.70, max 1.55) | Farhadifar vertex model of a 60 x 6 hexagonal PSM sheet (20 um pitch, Lambda_0 = 0.12, Gamma = 0.04, dLambda_cleft = 0.9, outer boundary pinned, gradient descent, no T1) in which only posterior(-1)->anterior(+1) half-somite interfaces are loaded: 12 clefts at 100.0 um pitch, cleft angle 28.2 -> 10.3 deg (control 27.3), tortuosity 1.30 -> 1.03, shape index 3.76 | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on somite_embryo_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9605) plus a per-cleft luminance-minimum line fit giving an empirical cleft angle of 7.9 deg; transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior paraxial mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; the specimen is a chick SEM in pixels with no scale bar, so S_obs (px) is compared to the Cooke-Zeeman waveform shape and cleft orientation only, not to S_sim in um | The FGF/RA toggle parameters (alpha = 3, K = 1, n = 4, tau_FR = 12 min, k_dM = 0.0074/min) are tuned to place the front offset ~0.19 mm behind the tailbud; they are not Goldbeter et al.'s published kinetic constants, so only the qualitative predictions (bistability, v_front = v_tb, bead effect) are tested | The chi = +1 / -1 compartments of the cusp are read as anterior / posterior half-somites (Saga & Takeda 2001) to decide which interfaces are clefts; Cooke & Zeeman themselves did not make this identification; does_not_claim: The published 3-4 variable Goldbeter (2007) kinetics with explicit Cyp26 / Raldh2, quantitative reproduction of its hysteresis figures or of Dubrulle (2001) somite sizes, T1 transitions / epithelial rosette formation / apical constriction, the 90-degree Xenopus somite cell-block rotation, 3D epithelialisation mechanics, or explicit Delta-Notch intercellular delay coupling (Slots 022-023)]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21193>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)80451-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/254196a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35098552>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nphys3471> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.903"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "d58a084" .
}

